{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Abm]Fifteen dollars is my game,
[B]fifteen is my [F#]draw
[B]Randall Collins [C#]is my name,
in the [E]state of [F#][Abm]Arkansas
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C#]Rollin’ dice at the railroad yard
won’t get you too much [F#]jack
[B]Workin’ on that [E]section gang
will [B]surely [F#]break your [Abm]back
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Just hidin’ out by the water tanks,
where the shade is cool
Watchin’ that straw boss hunt for me,
ain’t nobody’s fool
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
They’re makin’ up a train in the Memphis yard,
the longest I ever saw
Goin’ to ride it down to Fairbanks,
down in Arkansas
{end_of_chorus}
